course: dictionary
lesson: 9494
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning is needed. «The barge-woman steers with the tiller» means she controls which way the boat goes, because the tiller is the handle that turns the rudder.
explain: To steer can also mean to guide a person or a talk in a certain direction. Steer clear of means keep away from something. If you steer clear of the ice, you stay off it.
explain: A steer is also a noun: a young male cow kept for meat. Informally, a steer is a hint or a piece of advice. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then try it there to check.
fact: Steer is a verb: steer, steers, steered, steering.
fact: «Steer» means to control which way a car, bike, boat or other vehicle goes.
fact: «Steer» can also mean to guide a person or a talk in a certain direction.
fact: A steer is a young male cow kept for meat, and informally it can mean a hint or a piece of advice.
fact: «Steer clear of» means keep away from something.
exercise: «The barge-woman steers with the tiller.» What does steer mean here? | *To control which way the boat goes | To eat slowly at a long table | To pull a barge along with a rope | To sleep with half a brain
exercise: Mia says, «Steer clear of the ice, it's slippery.» What does steer clear of mean? | Walk right out onto the ice to test it | Steer the ice to the shore | Spin round and round on the ice | *Keep away from the ice
exercise: «Pigs even steered a joystick with their snouts to play a game.» What does steer mean here? | To guide a pig into a pen | To make a loud squeal | To lift the snout up high | *To control the direction of a game controller
test: «The rails steer the wheels, so the driver can only make the train go faster or slower.» What does steer mean here? | Paint the wheels | *Control which way the wheels go | Make a loud noise | Stop the wheels from turning
test: Ella says, «Her friend gave me a steer on which book to read.» What is a steer here? | A steering wheel | A long flat boat | A young male cow | *A hint or piece of advice
exam: Which phrase means keep away from something? | *steer clear of | steer a joystick | steering wheel | steer the boat
